========================================================================
                 C++ PROJECT INSTALLATION & RUN GUIDE
========================================================================

Follow these step-by-step instructions to set up and run the project 
on your Windows computer.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 1: INSTALL REQUIRED SOFTWARE
------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Install VS Code:
   - Download and install Visual Studio Code (https://code.visualstudio.com/).

2. Install C/C++ Extension:
   - Open VS Code.
   - Go to Extensions (Ctrl + Shift + X).
   - Search for "C/C++" (by Microsoft) and click Install.

3. Install MinGW C++ Compiler:
   - Ensure you have MinGW (C++ compiler) installed on your system.
   - Make sure your MinGW "bin" folder (e.g., C:\mingw\bin or C:\msys64\mingw64\bin) 
     is added to your Windows System Environment Variables (PATH).
   - To verify: Open Command Prompt and type: g++ --version

------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 2: OPEN THE PROJECT IN VS CODE
------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Extract or download the project files onto your computer.
2. Launch VS Code.
3. Click "File" > "Open Folder..." and select the project folder.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 3: OPEN TERMINAL & NAVIGATE TO SOURCE FOLDER
------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Open the Integrated Terminal in VS Code:
   - Press `Ctrl + ~` or go to Terminal > New Terminal.
2. Ensure you are using PowerShell or Command Prompt (do not use WSL).
3. Navigate into the source code folder:
   
   cd src

------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 4: COMPILE AND RUN
------------------------------------------------------------------------
To compile all source files and run the program, paste and run the 
following command in your terminal:

g++ *.cpp -o main -lbgi -lgdi32 -lcomdlg32 -luuid -loleaut32 -lole32 ; .\main

------------------------------------------------------------------------
TROUBLESHOOTING / COMMON ISSUES
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Issue 1: "ld returned 1 exit status" / "Permission denied"
   - Cause: The program (main.exe) is already open in the background.
   - Fix: Close any running graphics or console windows generated by 
     the program, or run this in PowerShell to force-close it:

     Stop-Process -Name "main" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue

Issue 2: "undefined reference to..."
   - Cause: Only one .cpp file was compiled instead of all required source files.
   - Fix: Make sure to use `g++ *.cpp` instead of `g++ main.cpp`.

